VERDICT: PASS
===========================================================================
  A hardware MAC ACL and a hardware IPv6 ACL coexist on the same port
  (access-group 4000 + ipv6 traffic-filter v6mac, both accepted).

  "MAC entries match both IPv6 and non-IPv6"   -- PROVEN, the key claim:
      deny 0000.1111.2222 (exact mask), dst any
      IPv6 from that MAC  base 10/10 -> 0/10   DROPPED
      IPv4 from that MAC  base 10/10 -> 0/10   DROPPED
      IPv6 from another MAC              10/10 forwarded
      IPv4 from another MAC              10/10 forwarded
  The MAC rule is ethertype-agnostic, and traffic from a non-matching MAC is
  untouched by it.

  Syntax note: the hardware MAC ACL renders a full-ff destination mask as
  "any" -- `access-list 4000 deny 0000.1111.2222 0000.0000.0000
  0000.0000.0000 ffff.ffff.ffff` shows back as
  "4 deny 0000.1111.2222 0000.0000.0000 any".

